* ============================================================================
* LM723 behavioural macro-model  (ME5120 bench-supply project)
* ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
* TI publishes NO official SPICE model for the LM723 (TI E2E forum answer),
* so this model is built from the datasheet blocks [DS1 p.2 Equivalent Circuit]
* and tuned to the datasheet numbers it must reproduce:
*   VREF = 7.15 V typ                         [DS1 p.4, Reference Voltage]
*   Current limit 65 mA with RSC = 10 ohm     [DS1 p.4, Short Circuit Current Limit]
*   150 mA max output without external pass  [DS1 p.1, Features]
*   Standby current 1.7 mA                    [DS1 p.4, Standby Current Drain]
*   Min input-output differential 3.0 V       [DS1 p.4]
* Pin order:  V+  V-  VC  VOUT  VREF  NI  INV  COMP  CL  CS
* (DIP-14 pin numbers: V+=12 V-=7 VC=11 VOUT=10 VREF=6 NI=5 INV=4 COMP=13 CL=2 CS=3)
* ============================================================================
.subckt LM723 VP VM VC VOUT VREF NI INV COMP CL CS params: VR=7.15
* --- Reference: VR (default 7.15 V), collapses if V+ - V- is too low ---------
* VR can be set per instance for tolerance studies: LM723C 6.80 to 7.50 V [DS1 p.4]
Bref  nref VM V=min({VR}, max(V(VP,VM)-2.2, 0))
Rref  nref VREF 2
* --- Error amplifier: pull-up current into COMP, differential sink ----------
Ipu   VP COMP 0.6m
Bsink COMP VM I=0.6m*(1+tanh((V(INV)-V(NI))/0.04))*min(1, max(V(COMP,VM),0)/0.3)
Ro    COMP VM 5Meg
Cint  COMP VM 5p
* --- Series pass Darlington (VC -> VOUT), base driven from COMP -------------
Q1    VC COMP n1 QN723
Q2    VC n1 VOUT QN723
Rb12  n1 VOUT 10k
* --- Current-limit transistor: base CL, emitter CS, steals COMP drive -------
Q3    COMP CL CS QL723
* --- Quiescent (standby) current --------------------------------------------
Iq    VP VM 1.4m
.model QN723 NPN(IS=1e-15 BF=120 VAF=80 RB=10 RE=0.5)
.model QL723 NPN(IS=0.8e-14 BF=150 VAF=80)
.ends LM723
